{
  "title": "Aamaal of the Night of Arafah",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "اَللّٰهُمَّ یَا شَاهِدَ كُلِّ نَجْوٰی\nIt is recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer. It is narrated that Almighty Allah will forgive one who says this supplicatory prayer at the ‘Arafat Night or Friday nights:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ.\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHAAMANIR RAHEEM.\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ یَا شَاهِدَ كُلِّ نَجْوٰی\nALLAAHUMMA YAA SHAAHEDA KULLE NAJWAA \nO Allah Who witnesses all secrets of hearts, \nوَ مَوْضِعَ كُلِّ شَكْوٰی\nWA MAWZE-A’ KULLE SHAKWAA \nWho is the object of all complaints, \nوَ عَالِمَ كُلِّ خَفِیَّۃٍ\nWA A’AALEMA KULLE KHAFIYYATIN \nWho knows all hidden things, \nوَ مُنْتَهٰی كُلِّ حَاجَۃٍ\nWA MUNTAHAA KULLE HAAJTIN \nand Who is the aim of all needs! \nیَا مُبْتَدِئًا بِالنِّعَمِ عَلَی الْعِبَادِ\nWA MUBTA-DE-AN BIN-NE-A’ME A’LAL E’BAADE \nO He Who instigates favoring on the Servants! \nیَا كَریْمَ الْعَفْوِ \nYAA KAREEMAL A’FWE \nO He Who is All-generous in pardoning!\nیَا حَسْنَ التَّجَاوُزِ\nYAA HASANAT TAJAAWOZE \nO He Who is All-excellent in overlooking! \nیَا جَوَادُ یَا مَنْ لَا یُوَارِىْ مِنْهُ لَیْلٌ دَاجٍ\nYAA JAWAADO YAA MAN LAA YOWAAREE MINHO LAYLUN DAAJIN \nO All-magnanimous! O He Who cannot be concealed by the covering darkness of night, \nوَ لَا بَحْرٌ عَجَّاجٌ وَ لَا سَمَآءٌ ذَاتُ اَبْرَاجٍ\nWA LAA BAHRUN A’JJAAJUN WA LAA SAMAAA-UN ZAATO ABRAAJIN \nthe roaring clamor of oceans, the skies along with their constellations, \nوَ لَا ظُلَمٌ ذَاتُ ارْتِتَاجٍ\nWA LA ZOLAMUN ZAATUR TETAAJIN \nor the thunderous murk. \nیَا مَنِ الظُّلْمَۃُ عِنْدَهٗ ضِیَآءٌ\nYAA MANIZ ZULMATO I’NDAHU ZEYAAA-UN \nO He with Whom the entire murk is light, \nاَسْئَلُكَ بِنُوْرِ وَجْهِكَ الْكَرِیْمِ\nAS-ALOKA BE-NOORE WAJHEKAL KAREEMIL \nI beseech You in the name of the brightness of Your Noble Face \nالَّذِيْ تَجَلَّیْتَ بِهٖ لِلْجَبَلِ فَجَعَلْتَهٗ دَكًّا\nLAZEE TAJALLAYTA BEHI LIL-JABALE FA-JA-A’LTAHU DAKKAA \nthrough which You manifested Your glory to the mountain; so, You made it crumble \nوَ خَرَّ مُوْسٰی صَعِقًا \nWA KHARRA MOOSAA SA-E’QAA \nand (Prophet) Moses fell down in a swoon, \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ رَفَعْتَ بِهِ السَّمٰوٰتِ بِلَا عَمَدٍ\nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE RA-FA’TA BEHIS SAMAAWAATE BELAA A’MADIN \nin the name of Your Name by which You raised the heavens without any pillars \nوَ سَطَحْتَ بِهِ الْاَرْضَ عَلٰی وَجْهِ مَآءٍ جَمَدٍ\nWA SATAHTA BEHIL ARZA A’LAA WAJHE MAAA-IN JAMADIN \nand by which You flattened the earth on the surface of solid water, \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الْمَخْزُوْنِ الْمَكْنُوْنِ \nWA BISMEKAL MAKHZOONIL MAKNOONIL \nin the name of Your Name—the concealed, the stored, \nالْمَكْتُوْبِ الطَّاهِرِ الَّذِیْ \nMAKTOOBIT TAAHERIL LAZEE \nthe scribed, and the pure, which \nاِذَا دُعِیْتَ بِهٖ اَجَبْتَ \nEZAA DO-E’ETA BEHI AJABTA \nYou answer any one who beseeches You \nوَ اِذَا سُئِلْتَ بِهٖ اَعْطَیْتَ \nWA EZAA SO-ILTA BEHI A-A’TAYTA \nin its name and grant any one who asks You his request, \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ السُّبُوْحِ الْقُدُّوْسِ \nWA BISMEKAS SUBBOOHIL QUDDOOSIL \nin the name of Your Name; the Praised, Holy, \nالْبُرْهَانِ الَّذِیْ هُوَ نُوْرٌ عَلٰی كُلِّ نُوْرٍ \nBURHAANIL LAZEE HOWA NOORUN A’LAA KULLE NOORINW \nand Demonstrative, which is light over the entire light, \nوَّ نُوْرٌ مِنْ نُوْرٍ یُضِیْءُ مِنْهُ كُلُّ نُوْرٍ \nWA NOORUN MIN NOORIN YOZEE-O MINHO KULLO NOORIN \nwhich is light made of light, and from which all lights take their brightness; \nاِذَا بَلَغَ الْاَرْضَ انْشَقَّتْ \nEZAA BALAGHAL ARZAN SHAQQAT \nif it reaches the earth, it will be rent asunder, \nوَ اِذَا بَلَغَ السَّمٰوٰتِ فُتِحَتْ \nWA EZAA BALAGHAS SAMAAWAATE FOTEHAT \nif it reaches the heavens, they will be opened, \nوَ اِذَا بَلَغَ الْعَرْشَ اهْتَزَّ \nWA EZAA BALAGHAL A’RSHAH TAZZA \nand if it reaches the throne, it will quiver; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ تَرْتَعِدُ مِنْهُ فَرَائِصُ مَلٰٓئِكَتِكَ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE TARTA-E’DO MINHO FARAA-ESO MALAA-EKATEKA \nand in the name of Your Name from the fear of which the muscles of Your angels tremble. \nوَ اَسْئَلُكَ بِحَقِّ جَبْرَئِیْلَ وَ مِیْكَائِیْلَ وَ اِسْرَافِیْلَ \nWA AS-ALOKA BE-HAQQE JABRA-EELA WA MEEKAA-EELA WA ISRAAFEELA \nI beseech You in the name of [Archangels] Gabriel, Michael, and Seraph, \nوَ بِحَقِّ مُحَمَّدٍۨ الْمُصْطَفٰی \nWA BE-HAQQE MOHAMMADENIL MUSTAFAA \nin the name of Muhammad, the Divinely-chosen Prophet, \nصَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ \nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \npeace be upon him, his Household, \nوَ عَلٰی جَمِیْعِ الْاَنْبِیَآءِ وَ جَمِیْعِ الْمَلٰٓئِكَۃِ \nWA A’LAA JAMEE-I’L AMBEYAA-E WA JAMEE-I’L MALAA-EKATE \nand all prophets and angels; \nوَ بِالْاِسْمِ الَّذِیْ مَشٰی بِهِ الْخَضِرُ عَلٰی قُلَلِ الْمَآءِ \nWA BIL-ISLMIL LAZEE MASHAA BEHIL KHAZERO A’LAA QOLALIL MAAA-E \nin the name of the Name through which al-Khizr could walk on waters \nكَمَا مَشٰی بِهٖ عَلٰی جُدَدِ الْاَرْضِ \nKAMAA MASHAA BEHI A’LAA JODADIL ARZE \njust as he used to walk on lands; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ فَلَقْتَ بِهِ الْبَحْرَ لِمُوْسٰی \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE FALAQTA BEHIL BAHRA LE-MOOSAA \nin the name of You Name through which You caused the sea to cleave asunder for Moses, \nوَ اَغْرَقْتَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَ قَوْمَهٗ \nWA AGHRAQTA FIR-A’WNA WA QAWMAHU \nYou drowned Pharaoh and his people, \nوَ اَنْجَیْتَ بِهٖ مُوْسَی بْنَ عِمْرَانَ وَ مَنْ مَعَهٗ \nWA ANJAYTA BEHI MOOSAB NA I’MRAANA WA MAN MA-A’HU \nand saved Moses, the son of Imran, and those who accompanied him; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ دَعَاكَ بِهٖ مُوْسَی بْنَ عِمْرَانَ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI MOOSAB NA I’MRAANA \nin the name of Your Name by which Moses, the son of Imran, \nمِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ الْاَیْمَنِ \nMIN JAANEBIT TOORIL AYMANE \nbesought You from the right slope of the Mount; \nفَاسْتَجَبْتَ لَهٗ وَ اَلْقَیْتَ عَلَیْهِ مَحَبَّۃً مِنْكَ \nFAS-TAJABTA LAHU WA ALQAYTA A’LAYHE MAHABBATAN MINKA \nso, You responded to him and cast down upon him love from You; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ بِهٖ اَحْیٰی عِیْسَی بْنُ مَرْیَمَ الْمَوْتٰی \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE BEHI AHYAA E’ESAB NO MARYAMAL MAWTAA \nin the name of Your Name by which Jesus, the son of Mary, brought life to the dead, \nوَ تَكَلَّمَ فِی الْمَهْدِ صَبِیًّا \nWA TAKALLAMA FIL MAHDE SABIYYAN \ncould speak while he was a child in the cradle, \nوَ اَبْرَءَ الْاَكْمَهَ وَ الْاَبْرَصَ بِاِذْنِكَ \nWA ABRA-AL AKMAHA WAL ABRASA BE-IZNEKA \nand healed the blind and the leprous by Your permission; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ دَعَاكَ بِهٖ حَمَلَۃُ عَرْشِكَ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI HAMALATO A’RSHEKA \nin the name of Your Name by which the bearers of Your Throne besought You \nوَ جَبْرَئِیْلُ وَ مِیْكَائِیْلُ وَ اِسْرَافِیْلُ \nWA JABRA-EELO WA MEEKAA-EELO WA ISRAAFEELO \nand so did Gabriel, Michael, Seraph, \nوَ حَبِیْبُكَ مُحَمَّدٌ صَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ \nWA HABEEBOKA MOHAMMADUN SALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \nMuhammad Your most beloved one (peace be upon him and upon his Household), \nوَ مَلَآئِكَتُكَ الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَ وَ اَنْبِیَآئُكَ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ \nWA MALAA-EKATOKAL MOQARRABOONA WA AMBEYAAA-OKAL MURSALOONA \nYour favorite angels, Your messaged Prophets, \nوَ عِبَادُكَ الصَّالِحُوْنَ مِنْ اَهْلِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرَضِیْنَ \nWA E’BAADOKAS SAALEHOONA MIN AHLIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARAZEENA \nand Your righteous servants from among the inhabitants of the heavens and the layers of the earth; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِی دَعَاكَ بِهٖ ذُو النُّوْنِ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI ZOON NOONE \nin the name of Your Name by which Zu’l-Nun (Prophet Jonah) besought You \nاِذْ ذَهَبَ مُغَاضِبًا فَظَنَّ اَنْ لَنْ نَقْدِرَ عَلَیْهِ \nIZ ZAHABA MOGHAAZEBAN FAZANNA AN LAN NAQDERA A’LAYHE \nwhen he departed in wrath: he imagined that You had no power over him, \nفَنَادٰی فِی الظُّلُمَاتِ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ \nFA-NAADAA FIZ ZOLOMAATE AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA \nbut he cried through the depths of darkness, “There is no god but You. \nسُبْحٰنَكَ اِنِّیْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِیْنَ \nSUBHAANAKA INNEE KUNTO MENAZ ZAALEMEEN. \nGlory be to You. I was indeed one of those who are wrong!” \nفَاسْتَجَبْتَ لَهٗ وَ نَجَّیْتَهٗ مِنَ الْغَمِّ \nFASTAJABTA LAHU WA NAJJAYTAHU MENAL GHAMME \nSo, You responded to him and delivered him from the grief \nوَ كَذٰلِكَ نُنْجِی الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ \nWA KAZAALEKA NUNJIL MOAMENEENA \nand thus do You deliver the believers; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الْعَظِیْمِ الَّذِیْ دَعَاكَ بِهٖ دَاوٗدُ \nWA BISMEKAL A’ZEEMIL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI DA-WOODA \nin the name of Your Great Name by which David besought You \nوَ خَرَّ لَكَ سَاجِدًا فَغَفَرْتَ لَهٗ ذَنْبَهٗ \nWA KHARRA LAKA SAAJEDAN FAHGAFARTA LAHU ZANBAHU \nand as he fell down prostrating himself to You, You rectified it for him; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ دَعَتْكَ بِهٖ اٰسِیَۃُ امْرَاَۃُ فِرْعَوْنَ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’TKA BEHI AASEYATUM RA-ATO FIR-A’WNA \nin the name of Your Name by which Aasiyah, the wife of Pharaoh, besought You, \nاِذْ قَالَتْ رَبِّ ابْنِ لِیْ عِنْدَكَ بَیْتًا فِی الْجَنَّۃِ \nIZ QAALAT RABBIB NE LEE I’NDAKA BAYTAN FIL JANNATE \nsaying, “My Lord! Build for me a house with You in Paradise, \nوَ نَجِّنِیْ مِنْ فِرْعَوْنَ وَ عَمَلِهٖ \nWA NAJJENEE MIN FIR-A’WNA WA A’MALEHI \ndeliver me from Pharaoh and his doing, \nوَ نَجِّنِیْ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِیْنَ \nWA NAJJENEE MENAL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEENA \nand deliver me from the unjust people.” \nفَاسْتَجَبْتَ لَهَا دُعَائَهَا \nFASTAJABTA LAHAA DO-A’A-AHAA \nSo, You responded to her prayer; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ دَعَكَ بِهٖ اَیُوْبُ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI AYYOOBO \nin the name of Your Name by which (Prophet) Job \nاِذْ حَلَّ بِهِ الْبَلَآءُ فَعَافَیْتَهٗ \nIZ HALLA BEHIL BALAA-O FA-A’AFAYTAHU \nbesought You after misfortune had befallen him; \nوَ اٰتَیْتَهٗ اَهْلَهٗ وَ مِثْلَهُمْ مَعَهُمْ \nWA AATAYTAHU AHLAHU WA MISLAHUM MA-A’HUM \nso, You healed him and gave him his family and the like of them with them: \nرَحْمَۃً مِّنْ عِنْدِكَ وَ ذِكْرٰی لِلْعَابِدِیْنَ \nRAHMATAM MIN I’NDEKA WA ZIKRAA LIL-A’ABEDEENA \na mercy from You and a reminder to the worshippers; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ دَعَاكَ بِهٖ یَعْقُوْبُ فَرَدَدْتَ عَلَیْهِ بَصَرَهٗ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI YA’QOOBO FA-RADADTA A’LAYHE BASARAHU \nin the name of Your Name by which (Prophet) Jacob besought You; so, You returned to him his sight \nوَ قُرَّۃَ عَیْنِهٖ یُوْسُفَ وَ جَمَعْتَ شَمْلَهٗ \nWA QURRATA A’YNEHI YOOSOFA WA JA-MA’TA SHAMLAHU \nand the delight of his heart, Joseph, and You reunified him; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ دَعَاكَ بِهٖ سُلَیْمَانُ فَوَهَبْتَ لَهٗ مُلْكًا \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI SOLAYMAANO FA-WAHABTA LAHU MULKAL \nin the name of Your Name by which (Prophet) Solomon besought You; so, You gifted him kingdom \nلَّا یَنْبَغِیْ لِاَحَدٍ مِنْ بَعْدِهٖ \nLAA YANBAGHEE LE-AHADIN MIM BA’DEHI \nthat none else should never gain, \nاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْوَهَابُ \nINNAKA ANTAL WAHHAABO \nfor You are verily the Granter of bounties; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ سَخَّرْتَ بِهِ الْبُرَاقَ لِمُحَمَّدٍ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE SAKHKHARTA BEHIL BORAAQA LE-MOHAMMADIN \nin the name of Your Name by which You subdued the Buraq to Muhammad, \nصَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ وَ سَلَّمَ \nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WAA LAAHI WA SALLAAMA \npeace and blessings be upon him and his Household, \nاِذْ قَالَ تَعَالٰی سُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ اَسْرٰی بِعَبْدِهٖ \nIZ QAALA TA-A’ALAA SUBHAANAL LAZEE ASRAA BE-A’BDEHI \nas Almighty Allah says, “Glory be to Him Who made His servant \nلَیْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اِلَی الْمَسْجِدِ الْاَقْصٰی \nLAYLAM MENAL MASJEDIL HARAAME ELAL MASJEDIL AQSAA \nto go on a night from the Sacred Mosque to the remote mosque.” \nوَ قَوْلُهٗ سُبْحَانَ الَّذِیْ سَخَّرَ لَنَا هٰذَا \nWA QAWLOHU SUBHAANAL LAZEE SAKHKHARA LANAA HAAZAA \nHe also says, “Glory be to Him Who made this subservient to us \nوَ مَا كُنَّا لَهٗ مُقْرِنِیْنَ وَ اِنَّا اِلٰی رَبِّنَا لَمُنْقَلِبُوْنَ \nWA MAA KUNNA LAHU MUKRENEENA WA INNAA ELAA RABBENAA LA-MUNQALEBOONA \nand we were not able to do it. Surely, to our Lord we must return;” \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ تَنَزَّلَ بِهٖ جَبْرَئِیْلُ عَلٰی مُحَمَّدٍ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE TANAZZALA BEHI JABRA-EELO A’LAA MOHAMMADIN \nin the name of Your Name by which (Archangel) Jibraeel used to ascend to Muhammad, \nصَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ \nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \npeace be upon him and his Household; \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ دَعَاكَ بِهٖ اٰدَمُ \nWA BISMEKAL LAZEE DA-A’AKA BEHI AADAMO \nand in the name of Your Name by which Adam besought You; \nفَغَفَرْتَ لَهٗ ذَنْۢبَهٗ وَ اَسْكَنْتَهٗ جَنَّتَكَ \nFA-GHAFARTA LAHU ZAMBAHU WA ASKANTAHU JANNATAKA \nso, You rectified him and allowed him to dwell in Your Paradise. \nوَ اَسْئَلُكَ بِحَقِّ الْقُرْاٰنِ الْعَظِیْمِ \nWA AS-ALOKA BEHAQQIL QURAANIL A’ZEEME \nI beseech You in the name of the Great Qur'an, \nوَ بِحَقِّ مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِیِّیْنَ \nWA BE-HAQQE MOHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA \nin the name of Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets, \nوَ بِحَقِّ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَ بِحَقِّ فَصْلِكَ نَوْمَ الْقَضَآءِ \nWA BE-HAQQE IBRAAHEEMA WA BE-HAQQE FAZLEKA NAWMAL QAZAAA-E \nin the name of Abraham, in the name of Your Judgment on the Day of the Administration of Justice, \nوَ بِحَقِّ الْمَوَازِیْنِ اِذَا نُصِبَتْ \nWA BE-HAQQIL MAWAAZEENE EZAA NOSEBAT \nin the name of the Scales when they shall be set up, \nوَ الصُّحُفِ اِذَا نُشِرَتْ \nWAS SOHOFE EZAA NOSHERAT \nthe Scrolls when they shall be laid open, \nوَ بِحَقِّ الْقَلَمِ وَ مَا جَرٰی \nWA BE-HAQQIL QALAME WA MAA JARAA \nthe Pen and whatever has been decided, \nوَ اللَّوْحِ وَ مَا اَحْصٰی \nWAL-LAWHE WA MAA AHSAA \nand the Tablet and whatever it has recorded; \nوَ بِحَقِّ الْاِسْمِ الَّذِیْ كَتَبْتَهٗ عَلٰی سُرَادِقِ الْعَرْشِ \nWA BE-HAQQIL ISMIL LAZEE KATABTAHU A’LAA SORAADEQIL A’RSHE \nin the name of the Name that You had inscribed on the pavilion of the Divine Throne \nقَبْلَ خَلْقِكَ الْخَلْقَ وَ الدُّنْیَا وَ الشَّمْسَ وَ الْقَمَرَ بِاَلْفَیْ عَامٍ \nQABLA KHALQEKAL KHALQA WAD DUNYAA WASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA BE-ALFAY A’AMIN \ntwo thousand years before You created the beings, the world, the sun, and the moon. \nوَ اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَهٗ \nWA ASH-HADO AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU \nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner, \nوَ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ \nWA ANNA MOHAMMADAN A’BDOHU WA RASOOLOHU \nand that Muhammad is his servant and messenger. \nوَ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الْمَخْزُوْنِ فِیْ خَزَائِنِكَ \nWA AS-ALOKA BISMEKAL MAKHZOONE FEE KHAZAA-ENEKAL \nI beseech You in the name of Your Name that is hoarded in Your stores, \nالَّذِیْ اسْتَاْثَرْتَ بِهٖ فِیْ عِلْمِ الْغَیْبِ عِنْدَكَ \nLAZIS TAASARTA BEHI FEE I’LMIL GHAYBE I’NDAKA \nYou have kept in the knowledge of the Unseen with You \nلَمْ یَظْهَرْ عَلَیْهِ اَحَدٌ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ \nLAM YAZHAR A’LAYHE AHADUN MIN KAHLQEKA \nand it has not been shown to any of Your creatures, \nلَا مَلَكٌ مُّقَرَّبٌ وَّ لَا نَبِیٌّ مُرْسَلٌ \nLAA MALAKUM MOQARRABUNW WA LAA NABIYYUN MURSALUNW \nbe him a favorite angel, a missioned Prophet, \nوَّ لَا عَبْدٌ مُصْطَفًی \nWA LAA A’BDUN MUSTAFAA \nor a chosen servant. \nوَ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ شَقَقْتَ بِهِ الْبِحَارَ \nWA AS-ALOKA BISMEKAL LAZEE SHAQAQTA BEHIL BEHAARA \nI beseech You in the name of Your Name by which You rent asunder the oceans, \nوَ قَامَتْ بِهِ الْجِبَالُ \nWA QAAMAT BEHIL JEBAALO \nthe mountains rose, \nوَ اخْتَلَفَ بِهِ اللَّیْلُ وَ النَّهَارُ \nWAKH TALABA BEHIL LAYLO WAN NAHAARO \nand night and day follow each other, \nوَ بِحَقِّ السَّبْعِ الْمَثَانِیْ \nWA BE-HAQQIS SAB-I’L MASAANEE \nin the name of the seven of the oft-repeated verses \nوَ الْقُرْاٰنِ الْعَظِیْمِ \nWAL QURAANIL A’ZEEME \nand the Grand Qur'an, \nوَ بِحَقِّ الْكِرَامِ الْكَاتِبِیْنَ \nWA BE-HAQQIL KERAAMIL KAATEBEENA \nin the name of the noble, recording angels, \nوَ بِحَقِّ طٰهٰ وَ يٰسٓ  وَ كٓهٰيٰعٓصٓ\nWA BE-HAQQE TAAHAA WA YAASEEN WA KAAF-HAA-YAA-A’YN-SAAD \nin the name of Ta-Ha, Ya-Sin, Kaf-Ha-Ya-Ayn-Sad, \nوَ حٰم عٓسٓقٓ وَ بِحَقِّ تَوْرَیْۃِ مُوْسٰی \nWA HAA-MEEM-A’YN-SEEN-QAAF WA BE-HAQQE TAWRAYTE MOOSAA \nHa-Mim-Ayn-Sin-Qaf, and in the name of the Torah of Moses, \nوَ اِنْجِیْلِ عِیْسٰی وَ زَبُوْرِ دَاوٗدَ \nWA INJEELE E’ESAA WA ZABOORE DA-WOODA \nthe Gospel of Jesus, the Psalms of David, \nوَ فُرْقَانِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nWA FURQAANE MOHAMMADIN \nthe Furqan (Criterion) of Muhammad, \nصَلَّی اللهُ عَلَیْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ \nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI \npeace be upon him, his Household, \nوَ عَلٰی جَمِیْعِ الرُّسُلِ وَ بَاهِیَا شَرَاهِیَا \nWA A’LAA JAMEE-I’R ROSOLE WA BAAHEYAA SHARAA-HEYAA \nand all the messengers and baaheyaa sharaaheyaa \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِحَقِّ تِلْكَ الْمُنَاجَاتِ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA BE-HAQQE TILKAL MONAAJAATIL \nO Allah, I beseech You in the name of this confidential talk \nالَّتِیْ كَانَتْ بَیْنَكَ وَ بَیْنَ مُوْسَی بْنِ عِمْرَانَ \nLATEE KAANAT BAYNAKA WA BAYNA MOOSAB NE I’MRAANA \nwhich took place between You and Moses, the son of Imran, \nفَوْقَ جَبَلِ طُوْرِ سَیْنَاءَ \nFAWQA JABALE TOORE SAYNAA-A \non the Mount Tur Sayna’, \nوَ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِی عَلَّمْتَهٗ مَلَكَ الْمَوْتِ \nWA AS-ALOKA BISMEKAL LAZEE A’LLAMTAHU MALAKAL MAWTE \nI beseech You in the name of Your Name which You taught the Angel of Death \nلِقَبْضِ الْاَرْوَاحِ \nLE-QABZIL ARWAAHE \nso that he would be able to grasp the souls, \nوَ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ كُتِبَ عَلٰی وَرَقِ الزَّیْتُوْنِ \nWA AS-ALOKA BISMEKAL LAZEE KOTEBA A’LAA WARAQIZ ZAYTOONE\nI beseech You in the name of Your Name which was written on the leaves of olive-trees; \nفَخَضَعَتِ النِّیْرَانُ لِتِلْكَ الْوَرَقَۃِ \nFA-KHAZA-A’TIN NEERAANO LE-TILKAL WARAQATE \nso, fires subdued to these leaves \nفَقُلْتَ یَا نَارُ كُوْنِیْ بَرْدًا وَّ سَلَامًا \nFA-QULTA YAA NAARO KOONEE BARDANW WA SALAAMAN \nafter You said, “O fire! Be a comfort and peace,” \nوَ اَسْئَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِیْ كَتَبْتَهٗ \nWA AS-ALOKA BISMEKAL LAZEE KATABTAHU \nand I beseech You in the name of Your Name that You wrote \nعَلٰی سُرَادِقِ الْمَجْدِ وَ الْكَرَامَۃِ \nA’LAA SORAADEQIL MAJDE WAL KARAAMATE \non the canopies of Glory and Dignity. \nیَا مَنْ لَا یُحْفِیْهِ سَآئِلٌ \nYAA MAN LAA YOHFEEHE SAAA-ELUN \nO He Who cannot be annoyed by any beseecher, \nوَ لَا یَنْقُصُهٗ نَآئِلٌ \nWA LAA YANQOSOHU NAAA-ELUN \nHe Who cannot be influenced by any reward! \nیَا مَنْ بِهٖ یُسْتَغَاثُ وَ اِلَیْهِ یُلْجَاءُ \nYAA MAN BEHI YUSTAGHAASO WA ELAYHE YULJAA-O \nO He Whose refuge is taken and to Whom resort is made! \nاَسْئَلُكَ بِمَعَاقِدِ الْعِزِّ مِنْ عَرْشِكَ \nAS-ALOKA BE-MA-A’AQEDIL I’ZZE MIN A’RSHEKA \nI beseech You in the name of the Seats of Honor belonging to Your Throne, \nوَ مُنْتَهَی الرَّحْمَۃِ مِنْ كِتَابِكَ \nWA MUNTAHAR RAHMATE MIN KETAABEKA \nthe utmost of mercy in Your Book, \nوَ بِاسْمِكَ الْاَعْظَمِ وَ جَدِّكَ الْاَعْلٰی \nWA BISMEKAL A-A’ZAME WA JADDEKAL A-A’LAA \nYour All-great Name, Your All-high majesty, \nوَ كَلِمَاتِكَ التَّامَّاتِ الْعُلٰی \nWA KALEMAATEKAT TAAMMAATIL O’LAA \nand Your most high, perfect Words. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ الرِّیَاحِ وَ مَا ذَرَتْ \nALLAAHUMMA RABBAR REYAAHE WA MAA ZARAT \nO Allah, Lord of winds and whatever they scatter far, \nوَ السَّمَآءِ وَ مَا اَظَلَّتْ \nWAS SAMAAA-E WA MAA AZALLAT \nLord of the sky and whatever it covers, \nوَ الْاَرْضِ وَ مَا اَقَلَّتْ \nWAL ARZE WA MAA AQALLAT \nthe Lord of the earth and whatever it carries, \nوَ الشَّیَاطِیْنِ وَ مَا اَضَلَّتْ \nWASH SHAYAATEENE WA MAA AZALLAT \nthe Lord of the devils and whomever they mislead, \nوَ الْبِحَارِ وَ مَا جَرَتْ \nWAL BEHAARE WA MAA JARAT \nand the Lord of the oceans and wherever they flow. \nوَ بِحَقِّ كُلِّ حَقٍّ هُوَ عَلَیْكَ حَقٌّ \nWA BE-HAQQE KULLE HAQQIN HOWA A’LAYKA HAQQUN \nI beseech You in the name of everything that enjoys a right with You, \nوَ بِحَقِّ الْمَلٰٓئِكَۃِ الْمُقَرَّبِیْنَ \nWA BE-HAQQE MALAA-EKATIL MOQARRABEENA \nin the name of the favorite angels, \nوَ الرَّوْحَانِیِّیْنَ وَ الْكَرُّوْبِیِّیْنَ \nWAR RAWHAANIYYEENA WAL KARROOBIYYEENA \nthe angels managing the spirits, the cherubim, \nوَ الْمُسَبِّحِیْنَ لَكَ بِاللَّیْلِ وَ النَّهَارِ لَا یَفْتُرُوْنَ \nWAL MOSABBEHEENA LAKA BIL-LAYLE WAN NAHAARE LAA YAFTOROONA \nand the angels praising You night and day without showing sluggishness, \nوَ بِحَقِّ اِبْرَاهِیْمَ خَلِیْلِكَ \nWA BEHAQQE IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELEKA \nin the name of Abraham, Your intimate friend, \nوَ بِحَقِّ كُلِّ وَ لِیٍّ یُّنَادِیْكَ بَیْنَ الصَّفَا وَ الْمَرْوَۃِ \nWA BE-HAQQE KULLE WALIYYIN YONAADEEKA BAYNAS SAFAA WAL MARWATE \nand in the name of each and every saint who calls You between Safa and Marwah \nوَ تَسْتَجِیْبُ لَهٗ دُعَآئَهٗ یَا مُجِیْبُ \nWA TASTAJEEBO LAHU DO-A’AA-AHU YAA MOJEEBO \nAnd You grant him his prayer, O Granter of prayers.\nاَسْئَلُكَ بِحَقِّ هٰذِهِ الْاَسْمَآءِ \nAS-ALOKA BE-HAQQE HAAZEHIL ASMAAA-E \nI beseech You in the name of all these names \nوَ بِهٰذِهِ الدَّعْوَاتِ \nWA BE-HAAZEHID DA’WAATE \nand all these prayers \nاَنْ تَغْفِرَ لَنَا مَا قَدَّمْنَا وَ مَا اَخَّرْنَا \nAN TAGHFERA LANAA MAA QADDAMNAA WA MAA AKHKHARNAA \nto forgive us all our past and coming sins, \nوَ مَا اَسْرَرْنَا وَ مَا اَعْلَنَّا \nWA MAA ASRARNAA WA MAA A-A’LANNAA \nincluding the secret and the open, \nوَ مَا اَبْدَیْنَا وَ مَا اَخْفَیْنَا \nWA MAA ABDAYNAA WA MAA AKHFAYNAA \nthe hidden and the public, \nوَ مَا اَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهٖ مِنَّا \nWA MAA ANTA A-A’LAMO BEHI MINNAA \nand those whom You know better than we do. \nاِنَّكَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ \nINNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nVerily, You have power over all things. \nبِرَحْمَتِكَ یَا اَرْحَمْ الرَّاحِمِیْنَ \nBE-RAHMATEKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA \nIn the name of Your mercy, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy.\nیَا حَافِظَ كُلِّ غَرِیْبٍ یَا مُوْنِسَ كُلِّ وَحِیْدٍ \nYAA HAAFEZA KULLE GHAREEBIN YAA MOONESA KULLE WAHEEDIN \nO He Who guards all strangers! O He Who brings entertainment to all lonely ones!\nیَا قُوَّۃَ كُلِّ ضَعِیْفٍ یَا نَاصِرَ كُلِّ مَظْلُوْمٍ \nYAA QUWWATA KULLE ZA-E’EFIN YAA NAASERA KULLE MAZLOOMIN \nO He Who is the power of all the weak! O He Who is the support of all the persecuted!\nیَا رَازِقَ كُلِّ مَحْرُوْمٍ یَا مُوْنِسَ كُلِّ مُسْتَوْحِشٍ \nYAA RAAZEQA KULLE MAHROOMIN YAA MOONESA KULLE MUSTAWHESHIN \nO He Who bestows upon all the deprived! O He Who brings entertainment to all the lonesome!\nیَا صَاحِبَ كُلِّ مُسَافِرٍ یَا عِمَادَ كُلِّ حَاضِرٍ \nYAA SAAHEBA KULLE MOSAAFERIN YAA E’MAADA KULLE HAAZERIN \nO He Who is the company of all those on journeys! O He Who is the pillar of all the present!\nیَا غَافِرَ كُلِّ ذَنْبٍ وَّ خَطِیْئَۃٍ \nYAA GHAAFERA KULLE ZANBINW WA KHATEE-ATIN \nO He Who forgives all sins and offenses!\nیَا غِیَاثَ الْمُسْتَغِیْثِیْنَ \nYAA GHEYAASAL MUSTAGHEESEENA \nO He Who is the aid of all those begging aid!\nیَا صَرِیْخَ الْمُسْتَصْرِخِیْنَ \nYAA SAREEKAHL MUSTASREKHEENA \nO He Who is the relief of all those pleading for relief!\nیَا كَاشِفَ كَرْبِ الْمَكْرُوْبِیْنَ \nYAA KAASHEFA KARBIL MAKROOBEENA \nO He Who relieves the calamity of those inflicted with calamities!\nیَا فَارِجَ هَمِّ الْمَهْمُوْمِیْنَ \nYAA FAAREJA HAMMIL MAHMOOMEENA \nO He Who alleviate the distress of the distressed ones!\nیَا بَدِیْعَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرَضِیْنَ \nYAA BADEE-A’S SAMAAWAATE WAL ARAZEENA \nO He Who is the Originator of the heavens and the layers of the earth!\nیَا مُنْتَهٰی غَایَۃِ الطَّالِبِیْنَ \nYAA MUNTAHAA GHAAYATIT TAALEBEENA \nO He Who is the utmost hope of the seekers!\nیَا مُجِیْبَ دَعْوَۃِ الْمُضْطَرِّیْنَ \nYAA MOJEEBA DA’WATIL MUZ-TARREENA \nO He Who responds to the prayers of the troubled!\nیَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِیْنَ \nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEEN \nO He Who is the most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nیَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِیْنَ \nYAA RABBAL A’ALAMEENA \nO Lord of the worlds!\nیَا دَیَّانَ یَوْمِ الدِّیْنِ \nYAA DAYYAANA YAWMID DEENE \nO Master of the Judgment Day!\nیَا اَجْوَدَ الْاَجْوَدِیْنَ \nYAA AJWADAL AJWADEENA \nO most Magnanimous of all those who act magnanimously!\nیَا اَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِیْنَ \nYAA AKRAMAL AKRAMEENA \nO most Generous of all those who act generously!\nیَا اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِیْنَ \nYAA ASMA-A’S SAAME-E’ENA \nO most Hearing of all those who can hear!\nیَا اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِیْنَ \nYAA ABSARAN NAAZEREENA \nO most Seeing of all those who can see!\nیَا اَقْدَرَ الْقَادِرِیْنَ \nYAA AQDARAL QAADEREEN \nO most Powerful of all those who have power!\nاغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تُغَیِّرُ النِّعَمَ \nIGHFIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TOGHAYYERUN NE-A’MA \nforgive my sins that change the bounties\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تُوْرِثُ النَّدَمَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TOORESUN NADAMA \nAnd forgive me my sins that bring about remorse,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تُوْرِثُ السَّقَمَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TOORESUS SAQAMA \nforgive me my sins that result in ailment,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تَهْتِكُ الْعِصَمَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TAHTEKUL E’SAMA \nforgive me my sins that tear safeguards,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تَرُدُّ الدُّعَآءَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TARUDDUD DO-A’AA-A \nforgive me my sins that repel prayers,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تَحْبِسُ قَطْرَ السَّمَآءِ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TAHBESO QATRIS SAMAAA-E \nforgive me my sins that withhold the drops of the sky,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تُعَجِّلُ الْفَنَآءَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TO-A’JJELUL FANAAA-A \nforgive me my sins that hasten extinction,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تَجْلِبُ الشَّقَآءَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TAJLEBUSH SHAQAAA-A \nforgive me my sins that beget misery,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تُظْلِمُ الْهَوَآءَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TUZLEMUL HAWAAA-A \nforgive me my sins that darken the atmospheres,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ تَكْشِفُ الْغِطَآءَ \nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE TAKSHEFUL GHETAAA-A \nforgive me my sins that disclose the coverings,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِیَ الذُّنُوْبَ الَّتِیْ لَا یَغْفِرُهَا غَیْرُكَ یَا اَللهُ\nWAGH FIR LEYAZ ZONOOBAL LATEE LAA YAGHFEROHAA GHAYROKA YAA ALLAAHO\nforgive me my sins that none can forgive save You, O Allah,\nوَ احْمِلْ عَنِّیْ كُلَّ تَبِعَۃٍ لِّاَحَدٍ مِّنْ خَلْقِكَ \nWAH MIL A’NNEE KULLA TABE-A’TIL LE-AHADIM MIN KHALQEKA \nbear from me every offensive that I have made against any of Your creatures,\nوَ اجْعَلْ لِیْ مِنْ اَمْرِیْ فَرَجًا وَ مَخْرَجًا \nWAJ A’L LEE MIN AMREE FARAJAN WA MAKHRAJANW \nmake all my affairs reach at relief, exit, and easiness,\nوَّ یُسْرًا وَ اَنْزِلْ یَقِیْنَكَ فِیْ صَدْرِیْ \nWA YUSRAN WA ANZIL YAQEENAKA FEE SADREE \nmake Your tranquility ascend on my chest,\nوَ رَجَآئَكَ فِیْ قَلْبِیْ حَتّٰی لَا اَرْجُوْ غَیْرَكَ \nWA RAJAAA-AKA FEE QALBEE HATTAA LAA ARJOWA GHAYRAKA \nand make hope in You ascend on my heart so that I shall never hope for anyone save You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ احْفَظْنِیْ وَ عَافِنِیْ فِیْ مَقَامِیْ \nALLAAHUMMAH FAZNEE WA A’AFENEE FEE MAQAAMEE \nO Allah, safeguard me, heal me in all my situations,\nوَ اصْحَبْنِیْ فِیْ لَیْلِیْ وَ نَهَارِیْ \nWAS HABNEE FEE LAYLEE WA NAHAAREE \nbe my companion at nights and days,\nوَ مِنْۢ بَیْنِ یَدَیَّ وَ مِنْ خَلْفِیْ \nWA MIM BAYNE YADAYYA WA MIN KHALFEE \nbe ahead of me, behind me,\nوَ عَنْ یَمِیْنِیْ وَ عَنْ شِمَالِیْ \nWA A’N YAMEENEE WA A’N SHEMAALEE \nfrom my right side, from my left side,\nوَ مِنْ فَوْقِیْ وَ مِنْ تَحْتِیْ \nWA MIN FAWQEE WA MIN TAHTEE \nfrom above me, and from beneath me,\nوَ یَسِّرْ لِیَ السَّبِیْلَ وَ اَحْسِنْ لِیَ التَّیْسِیْرَ \nWA YASSIR LEYASSABEELA WA AHSIN LEYAT TAYSEERA \nmake easy all the ways for me, make excellent facilitation for me,\nوَ لَا تَخْذُلْنِیْ فِیْ الْعَسِیْرِ \nWA LAA TAKHZULNEE FIL A’SEERE \ndo not disappoint me in hardships,\nوَ اهْدِ نِیْ یَا خَیْرَ دَلِیْلٍ \nWAH DENEE YAA KHAYRA DALEELIN \nguide me, O Best of all guides,\nوَ لَا تَكِلْنِیْ اِلٰی نَفْسِیْ فِی الْاُمُوْرِ \nWA LAA TAKILNEE ELAA NAFSEE FIL OMOORE \ndo not leave me alone in all my affairs,\nوَ لَقِّنِیْ كُلَّ سُرُوْرٍ \nWA LAQQENEE KULLA SOROORIN \nmake me receive all pleasures,\nوَ اقْلِبْنِیْ اِلٰی اَهْلِیْ بِالْفَلَاحِ وَ النَّجَاحِ \nWAQ LIBNEE ELAA AHLEE BIL-FALAAHE WAN NAJAAHE \nand make me return to my family with prosperity, success,\nمَحْبُوْرًا فِی الْعَاجِلِ وَ الْاٰجِلِ \nMAHBOORAN FIL A’AJELE WA AAJELE \nand gladness in the present and in the future.\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ \nINNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nVerily, You have power over all things.\nوَ ارْزُقْنِیْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ \nWAR ZUQNEE MIN FAZLEKA \nbestow upon me with Your favors,\nوَ اَوْسِعْ عَلَیَّ مِنْ طَیِّبَاتِ رِزْقِكَ \nWA AWSE’ A’LAYYA MIN TAYYEBAATE RIZQEKA \nexpand for me the most favorable of Your sustenance,\nوَ اسْتَعْمِلْنِیْ فِیْ طَاعَتِكَ \nWAS TA’MILNEE FEE TAA-A’TEKA \napply me to the obedience to You,\nوَ اَجِرْنِیْ مِنْ عَذَابِكَ وَ نَارِكَ \nWA AJIRNEE MIN A’ZAABEKA WA NAAREKA \nredeem me from Your chastisement and Fire,\nوَ اقْلِبْنِیْ اِذَا تَوَفَّیْتَنِیْ اِلٰی جَنَّتِكَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ \nWAQ LIBNEE EZAA TAWAFFAYTANEE ELAA JANNATEKA BE-RAHMATEKA \nand when You grasp my soul, lead me to Your Paradise, by Your mercy.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ زَوَالِ نِعْمَتِكَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A-O’OZO BEKA MIN ZAWAALE NE’MATEKA \nO Allah, I seek Your protection against confiscation of Your graces,\nوَ مِنْ تَحْوِیْلِ عَافِیَتِكَ \nWA MIN TAHWEELE A’AFEYATEKA \nagainst alternation of Your conferral of wellbeing on me,\nوَ مِنْ حُلُوْلِ نَقِمَتِكَ \nWA MIN HOLOOLE NA-QEMATEKA \nagainst the befalling of Your punishment,\nوَ مِنْ نُزُوْلِ عَذَابِكَ \nWA MIN NOZOOLE A’ZAABEKA \nand against the ensuing of Your chastisement.\nوَ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ جَهْدِ الْبَلَآءِ \nWA A-O’OZO BEKA MIN JAHDIL BALAAA-E \nI seek Your protection against arduous hardships,\nوَ دَرَكِ الشَّقَآءِ \nWA DARAKISH SHAQAAA-E \nagainst coming about of misery,\nوَ مِنْ سُوْٓءِ الْقَضَآءِ \nWA MIN SOOO-IL QAZAAA-E \nagainst evil end results, \nوَ شَمَاتَۃِ الْاَعْدَآءِ \nWA SHAMAATATIL A-A’DAAA-E \nagainst my enemies’ gloating over my grief,\nوَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا یَنْزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ \nWA MIN SHARRE MAA YANZELO MENAS SAMAAA-E \nagainst the evil of everything that ascends from the heavens,\nوَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا فِیْ الْكِتَابِ الْمُنْزَلِ \nWA MIN SHARRE MAA FIL KETAABIL MUNZALE \nand against the evils mentioned in the Revealed Book.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تَجْعَلْنِیْ مِنَ الْاَشْرَارِ \nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAJ-A’LNEE MENAL ASHRAARE \nO Allah, do not include me with the evil ones,\nوَ لَا مِنْ اَصْحَابِ النَّارِ \nWA LAA MIN ASHAABIN NAARE \ndo not include me with the people of Hellfire,\nوَ لَا تَحْرِمْنِیْ صُحْبَۃَ الْاَخْیَارِ \nWA LAA TAHRIMNEE SOHBATAL AKHYAARE \ndo not deprive me of the companionship of the upright people,\nوَ اَحْیِنِیْ حَیٰوۃً طَیِّبَۃً \nWA AHYENEE HAYAATAN TAYYEBATAN \ngrant me a pleasant lifetime,\nوَ تَوَفَّنِیْ وَفَاۃً طَیِّبَۃً \nWA TAWAFFANEE WAFAATAN TAYYEBATAN \ndecide for me a kind of death \nتُلْحِقُنِیْ بِالْاَبْرَارِ \nTULHEQONEE BIL-ABRAARE \ndue to which You will join me to the Pious Ones,\nوَ ارْزُقْنِیْ مُرَافَقَۃَ الْاَنْبِیَآءِ\nWAR ZUQNEE MORAAFAQATAL AMBEYAAA-E \nand confer upon me with the companionship of the Prophets\nفِیْ مَقْعَدِ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ مَلِیْكٍ مُقْتَدِرٍ \nFEE MAQ-A’DE SIDQIN I’NDA MALEEKIN MUQTADERIN \nin the seat of honesty with the All-powerful King.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلٰی حُسْنِ بَلَآئِكَ \nALLAAHUMMA LAKAL HAMDO A’LAA HUSNE BALAAA-EKA \nO Allah, all praise be to You for Your pleasant trials and deeds to us.\nوَ صُنْعِكَ وَ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلَی الْاِسْلَامِ \nWA SUN-E’KA WA LAKAL HAMDO A’LAL ISLAAME \nAll praise be to You for my being Muslim \nوَ اتِّبَاعِ السُّنَّۃِ \nWAT TE-BAA-I’S SUNNATE \nand for my following the Prophet’s traditions.\nیَا رَبِّ كَمَا هَدَیْتَهُمْ لِدِیْنِكَ \nYAA RABBE KAMAA HADAYTAHUM LE-DEENEKA \nO my Lord, as You have guided them (i.e. the pious)\nوَ عَلَّمْتَهُمْ كِتَابَكَ فَاهْدِنَا وَ عَلِّمْنَا \nWA A’LLAMTAHUM KETAABAKA FAHDENAA WA A’LLIMNAA \nand taught them Your Book, (please) guide us and teach us.\nوَ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلٰی حُسْنِ بَلَآئِكَ \nWA LAKAL HAMDO A’LAA HUSNE BALAAA-EKA \nAll praise be to You for Your pleasant trials \nوَ صُنْعِكَ عِنْدِیْ خَاصَّۃً كَمَا خَلَقْتَنِیْ فَاَحْسَنْتَ خَلْقِیْ \nWA SUN-E’KA I’NDEE KHAASSATAN KAMAA KHALAQTANEE FA-AHSANTA KHALQEE \nand deeds to me in private, as You created me, gifted me an excellent form,\nوَ عَلَّمْتَنِیْ فَاَحْسَنْتَ تَعْلِیْمِیْ \nWA A’LLAMTANEE FA-AHSANTA TA’LEEMEE \ntaught me, gifted me excellent erudition,\nوَ هَدَیْتَنِیْ فَاَحْسَنْتَ هِدَایَتِیْ \nWA HADAYTANEE FA-AHSANTA HEDAAYATEE \nguided me, and gifted me excellent guidance.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلٰی اِنْعَامِكَ عَلَیَّ \nFALAKAL HAMDO A’LAA IN-A’AMEKA A’LAYYA \nSo, all praise be to You for Your favors that You conferred upon me \nقَدِیْمًا وَّ حَدِیْثًا \nQADEEMANW WA HADEESAN \nin the past and in the present.\nفَكَمْ مِنْ كَرْبٍ یَا سَیِّدِیْ قَدْ فَرَّجْتَهٗ \nFAKAM MIN KARBIN YAA SAYYEDEE QAD FARRJATAHU \nToo many are the agonies that You, my Master, relieved.\nوَ كَمْ مِنْ غَمٍّ یَا سَیِّدِیْ قَدْ نَفَّسْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MIN GHAMMIN YAA SAYYEDEE QAD NAFFASTAHU \nToo many are the distresses that You, my Master, eased.\nوَ كَمْ مِنْ هَمٍّ یَا سَیِّدِیْ قَدْ كَشَفْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MIN HAMMIN YAA SAYYEDEE QAD KASHAFTAHU \nToo many are the sufferings that You, my Master, alleviated.\nوَ كَمْ مِّنْ بَلَآءٍ یَا سَیِّدِیْ قَدْ صَرَفْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MIN BALAAA-IN YAA SAYYEDEE QAD SARAFTAHU \nToo many are the hardships from which You, my Master, saved me.\nوَ كَمْ مِنْ عَیْبٍ یَا سَیِّدِیْ قَدْ سَتَرْتَهٗ \nWA KAM MAN A’YBIN YAA SAYYEDEE QAD SATARTAHU \nToo many are the defects that You, my Master, covered.\nفَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ عَلٰی كُلِّ حَالٍ \nFALAKAL HAMDO A’LAA KULLE HAALIN \nSo, all praise be to You for all conditions,\nفِیْ كُلِّ مَثْوًی وَّ زَمَانٍ\nFEE KULLE MASWANW WA ZAMAANIN\nin every place and time,\nوَ مُنْقَلَبٍ وَّ مَقَامٍ \nWA MUNQALABINW WA MAQAAMIN \nevery circumstance and situation,\nوَ عَلٰی هٰذِهِ الْحَالِ وَ كُلِّ حَالٍ \nWA A’LAA HAAZEHIL HAALE WA KULLE HAALIN \nand for the current condition and all conditions.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِیْ مِنْ اَفْضَلِ عِبَادِكَ \nALLAAHUMMAJ A’LNEE MIN AFZALE E’BAADEKA \nO Allah, shower upon me the best share of every good thing\nنَصِیْبًا فِیْ هٰذَ الْیَوْمِ مِنْ خَیْرٍ تَقْسِمُهٗ \nNASEEBAN FEE HAAZAL YAWME MIN KAHYRIN TAQSEMOHU \nthat You decide for Your servants on this day,\nاَوْ ضُرٍّ تَكْشِفُهٗ اَوْ سُوْءٍ تَصْرِفُهٗ \nAW ZURRIN TAKSHEFOHU AW SOO-IN TASREFOHU \nsuch as harm that You decide to hold off, evil that You decide to ward off,\nاَوْ بَلَآءٍ تَدْفَعُهٗ اَوْ خَیْرٍ تَسُوْقُهٗ \nAW BALAA-IN TAD-FA-O’HU AW KHAYRIN TASOOQOHU \nordeal that You decide to deter, grace that You decide to grant,\nاَوْ رَحْمَۃٍ تَنْشُرُهَا اَوْ عَافِیَۃٍ تُلْبِسُهَا \nAW RAHMATIN TANSHOROHAA AW A’AFEYATIN TULBESOHAA \nitem of mercy that You decide to distribute, and item of wellbeing that You decide to cover up (on one of Your servants),\nفَاِنَّكَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ \nFA-INNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nfor You verily have power over all things,\nوَ بِیَدِكَ خَزَآئِنُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ \nWA BE-YADEKA KHAZAAA-ENUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE \nin Your hands lie the hoards of the heavens and the earth,\nوَ اَنْتَ الْوَاحِدُ الْكَرِیْمُ الْمُعْطِی \nWA ANTAL WAAHEDUL KAREEMUL MO’TIL \nYou are verily the One, the All-generous, and the Best Bestower,\nالَّذِیْ لَا یُرَدُّ سَائِلُهٗ \nLAZEE LAA YORADDO SAA-ELOHU \nYou are the One Whose beseechers are not rejected,\nوَ لَا یُخَیَّبُ اٰمِلُهٗ \nWA YAA YOKHAYYABO AAMELOHU \nand You are the One Who never disappoint those who put hope in Him,\nوَ لَا یَنْقُصُ نَائِلُهٗ \nWA LAA YANQOSO NAA-ELOHU \nthe One Who is never influenced by the rewards that He bestows upon anyone,\nوَ لَا یَنْفَدُ مَا عِنْدَهٗ \nWA LAA YANFADO MAA I’NDAHU \nand the One Whose possessions never run out;\nبَلْ یَزْدَادُ كَثْرَۃً وَّ طَیِّبًا\nBAL YAZDAADO KASRATANW WA TAYYEBANW\nrather, You always increase in quantity, excellent gift,\nوَّ عَطَآءً وَّ جُوْدًا \nWA A’ATAAA-ANW WA JOODAN \nconferrals, and magnanimity.\nوَ ارْزُقْنِیْ مِنْ خَزَآئِنِكَ الَّتِیْ لَا تَفْنٰی \nWAR ZUQNEE MIN KHAZAAA-ENEKAL LATEE LAA TAFNAA \nbestow upon me from Your hoards that never come to an end\nوَ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ الْوَاسِعَۃِ \nWA MIN RAHMATEKAL WAA-SE-A’TE \nand from Your expansive mercy.\nاِنَّ عَطَآئَكَ لَمْ یَكُنْ مَّحْظُوْرًا \nINNA A’TAAA-AKA LAM YAKUM MAHZOORAN \nYour conferral shall never be confined\nوَ اَنْتَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدٍیْرٌ \nWA ANTA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nand You have power over all things;\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ یَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِیْنَ.\nBE-RAHMATEKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEEN.\nin the name of Your mercy; O most Merciful of all those who show mercy.",
  "merits": "This blessed night is the night of praying for granting all requests. Repentance at this night is accepted, prayers responded, and acts of worship and obedience achieve the reward of one hundred and seventy years of worship. ",
