    "اَللّٰهُمَّ مَنْ تَعَبَّاَ وَتَهَيَّاَ \nIt is recommended to say the supplication, dedicated to the ‘Arafat Day and the Friday nights and days, which is as follows:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ.\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHAAMANIR RAHEEM. \nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَنْ تَعَبَّاَ وَتَهَيَّاَ \nALLAAHUMMA MAN TA-A’BBA-A WA TAHAYYA-A \nO Allah, One may call up, prepare,\nوَ اَعَدَّ وَ اسْتَعَدَّ \nWA A-A’DDA WAS TA-A’DDA \nready oneself, and stand prepared\nلِوِفَادَةٍ اِلٰى مَخْلُوْقٍ \nLE-WEFAADATIN ELAA MAKHLOOQIN \nfor purpose of coming to a creature\nرَجَآءَ رِفْدِهٖ \nRAJAAA-A RIFDEHI \nin the hope of gaining his aid\nوَ طَلَبَ نَائِلِهٖ وَ جَائِزَتِهٖ \nWA TALABA NAA-ELEHI WA JAA-EZATEHI \nand asking for his gift and present.\nفَاِلَيْكَ يَا رَبِّ تَعْبِيَتِيْ وَ اسْتِعْدَادِيْ \nFA-ELAYKA YAA RABBE TA’BEYATEE WAS TEA’DAADEE \nAs for myself, to You—O my Lord—I make my preparations and readiness\nرَجَاءَ عَفْوِكَ \nRAJAAA-A A’FWEKA \nhoping for Your pardon\nوَ طَلَبَ نَائِلِكَ وَ جَائِزَتِكَ \nWA TALABA NAA-ELEKA WA JAAA-EZATEKA \nand asking for Your gift and present.\nفَلَا تُخَيِّبْ دُعَائِيْ \nFALAA TOKHAYYIB DO-A’AA-EE \nSo, do not disappoint my entreaty.\nيَا مَنْ لَا يَخِيْبُ عَلَيْهِ سَائِلٌ \nYAA MAN LAA YAKHEEBO A’LAYHE SAAA-ELUN \nO He Who never disappoints His beseechers\nوَ لَا يَنْقُصُهٗ نَائِلٌ \nWA LAA YANQOSOHU NAAA-ELUN\nand Whose prizes never decrease His ample-giving!\nفَاِنِّيْ لَمْ آتِكَ ثِقَةً بِعَمَلٍ صَالِحٍ عَمِلْتُهٗ \nFA-INNEE LAM AATEKA SEQATAN BE-A’MALIN SAALEHIN A’MILTOHU \nI have not come to You with confidence of a righteous deed that I have done\nوَ لَا لِوِفَادَةِ مَخْلُوْقٍ رَجَوْتُهٗ \nWA LAA LE-WEFAADATE MAKHLOOQIN RAJAWTOHU \nnor have I had any hope in a grant of any creature.\nاَتَيْتُكَ مُقِرًّا عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ بِالْاِسَائَةِ وَ الظُّلْمِ \nATAYTOKA MOQIRRAN A’LAA NAFSEE BIL-ESAAA-ATE WAZ ZULME \nRather, I have come to You professing myself to be evildoer and transgressor\nمُعْتَرِفُا بِاَنْ لَا حُجَّةَ لِيْ وَ لَا عُذْرَ \nMO’TAREFAN BE-AN LAA HUJJATA LEE WA LAA U’ZRA \nand confessing that I lack any pretext or excuse.\nاَتَيْتُكَ اَرْجُوْ عَظِيْمَ عَفْوِكَ \nATAYTOKA ARJOO A’ZEEMA A’FWEKAL \nI have come to You hoping for Your great pardon\nالَّذِيْ عَفَوْتَ بِهٖ عَنِ الْخَاطِئِيْنَ \nLAZEE A’FAWTA BEHI A’NIL KHAATE-EENA \ndue to which You have pardoned the wrongdoers.\nفَلَمْ يَمْنَعْكَ طُوْلُ عُكُوْفِهِمْ عَلٰي عَظِيْمِ الْجُرْمِ \nFALAM YAMNA’KA TOOLO O’KOOFEHIM A’LAA A’ZEEMIL JURME \nHence, their long-lasting retirement to their grave offenses has not prevented You\nاَنْ عُدْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِالرَّحْمَةِ \nAN U’DTA A’LAYHIM BIR-RAHMATE \nfrom turning to them with mercy.\nفَيَا مَنْ رَحْمَتُهٗ وَاسِعَةٌ \nFAYAA MAN RAHMATOHU WAASE-A’TUN \nO He Whose mercy is huge\nوَ عَفْوُهٗ عَظيْمٌ \nWA A’FWOHU A’ZEEMUN \nand Whose pardon is great;\nيَا عَظِيْمُ يَا عَظِيْمُ يَا عَظِيْمُ \nYAA A’ZEEMO YAA A’ZEEMO YAA A’ZEEMO \nO All-great, O All-great, O All-great;\nلَا يَرُدُّ غَضَبَكَ اِلَّا حِلْمُكَ \nLAA YARUDDO GHAZABAKA ILLAA HILMOKA \nnothing can repel Your rage except Your forbearance\nوَ لَا يُنْجِيْ مِنْ سَخَطِكَ اِلَّا التَّضَرُّعُ اِلَيْكَ \nWA LAA YUNJEE MIN SAKHATEKA ILLAAT TAZARRO-O’ ELAYKA \nand nothing can save from Your wrath except imploring earnestly to You.\nفَهَبْ لِيْ يَا اِلٰهِيْ فَرَجًا \nFAHAB LEE YAA ELAAHI FARAJAN \nSo, my God, grant me a relief\nبِالْقُدْرَةِ الَّتِيْ تُحْيِيْ بِهَا مَيْتَ الْبِلَادِ \nBIL-QUDRATIL LATEE TOHYEE BEHAA MAYTAL BELAADE \nin the name of the power through which You restore to life the derelict lands,\nوَ لَا تُهْلِكْنِيْ غَمًّا حَتّٰى تَسْتَجِيْبَ لِيْ \nWA LAA TOHLIKNEE GHAMMAN HATTAA TASTAJEEBA LEE \nand do not cause me to perish out of grief until You respond to me\nوَتُعَرِّفَنِيْ الْاِجَابَةَ فِيْ دُعَائِيْ \nWA TO-A’RREFANIL EJAABATA FEE DO-A’AA-EE \nand show me signs of Your response to my prayers.\nوَ اَذِقْنِيْ طَعْمَ الْعَافِيَةِ اِلٰى مُنَتَهٰى اَجَلِيْ \nWA AZIQNEE TA’MAL A’AFEYATE ELAA MUNTAHAA AJALEE \nMake me taste the flavor of wellbeing up to the end of my lifetime,\nوَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِيْ عَدُوِّيْ \nWA LAA TUSHMIT BEE A’DUWWEE \ndo not make my enemies gloat over me,\nوَ لَا تُسَلِّطْهُ عَلَيَّ \nWA LAA TOSALLITHO A’LAYYA \ndo not give them a hand over me,\nوَ لَا تُمَكِّنْهُ مِنْ عُنُقِيْ \nWA LAA TOMAKKINHO MIN O’NOQEE \nand do not make them control over me.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ وَضَعْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَرْفَعُنِيْ \nALLAAHUMMA IN WAZA’TANEE FAMAN ZAL LAZEE YARFA-O’NEE \nO Allah, If You humiliate me, who can then exalt me?\nوَ اِنْ رَفَعْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِيْ يَضَعُنِيْ \nWA IN RAFA’TANEE FAMAN ZAL LAZEE YAZA-O’NEE \nAnd if You exalt me, who can then humiliate me?\nوَ اِنْ اَهْلَكْتَنِيْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِيْ يَعْرِضُ لَكَ فِي عَبْدِكَ \nWA IN AHLAKTANEE FAMAN ZAL LAZEE YA’REZO LAKA FEE A’BDEKA \nIf You annihilate me, who can then interfere before You concerning the affair of me—Your slave\nاَوْ يَسْاَلُكَ عَنْ اَمْرِهٖ \nAW YAS-ALOKA A’N AMREHI \nor who can intercede to ask You about it?\nوَ قَدْ عَلِمْتُ اَنَّهٗ لَيْسَ فِي حُكْمِكَ ظُلْمٌ \nWA QAD A’LIMTO ANNAHU LAYSA FEE HUKMEKA ZULMUN \nI have already known for sure that Your decrees are devoid of injustice\nوَ لَا فِيْ نَقِمَتِكَ عَجَلَةٌ \nWA LAA FEE NAQEMATEKA A’JALATUN \nand Your punishment does not count on immediateness.\nوَ اِنَّمَا يَعْجَلُ مَنْ يَخَافُ الْفَوْتَ \nWA INNAMA YA’JELO MAN YAKHAAFUL FAWTA \nVerily, immediateness is the work of him who fears lest he may miss,\nوَ اِنَّمَا يَحْتَاجُ اِلَى الظُّلْمِ الضَّعِيْفُ \nWA INNAMAA YAHTAJO ELAZ ZULMIZ ZA-E’EFO \nand only do the weak need injustice.\nوَ قَدْ تَعَالَيْتَ يَا اِلٰهِيْ عَنْ ذٰلِكَ عُلُوًّا كَبِيْرًا \nWA QAD TA-A’ALAYTA YAA ELAAHI A’N ZAALEKA O’LUWWAN KABEERAN \nAs for You, O my God, You are too exalted to be so—Exalted and Great You are beyond all measure!\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ فَاَعِذْنِيْ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A-O’OZO BEKA FA-A-I’ZNEE \nO Allah, I take refuge in You; so, have protection upon me!\nوَ اَسْتَجِيْرُ بِكَ فَاَجِرْنِيْ \nWA ASTAJEERO BEKA FA-AJIRNEE \nI call for Your safekeeping; so, keep me under Your security!\nوَ اَسْتَرْزِقُكَ فَارْزُقْنِيْ \nWA ASTARZEQOKA FARZUQNEE \nI appeal for Your sustenance; so, provide me with sustenance!\nوَ اَتَوَكَّلُ عَلَيْكَ فَاكْفِنِيْ \nWA ATAWAKKALO A’LAYKA FAK-FENEE \nI put trust in You; so, keep me under Your supervision!\nوَ اَسْتَنْصِرُكَ عَلٰى عَدُوِّيْ فَانْصُرْنِيْ \nWA ASTANSEROKA A’LAA A’DUWWEE FANSURNEE \nI call for Your aid against my enemy; so, grant me support!\nوَ اَسْتَعِيْنُ بِكَ فَاَعِنِّيْ \nWA ASTA-E’ENO BEKA FA-A-I’NNEE \nI seek Your assistance; so, assist me!\nوَ اَسْتَغْفِرُكَ يَا اِلٰهِيْ فَاغْفِرْ لِيْ \nWA ASTAGHFEROKA YAA ELAAHI FAGH-FIR LEE \nI ask for Your forgiveness; so, forgive me.\nآمِيْنَ آمِيْنَ آمِيْنَ.\nAAMEENA AAMEENA AAMEENA.\nSo, respond! Respond! Respond!",
    "More Aamaal\n1. It is recommended to repeat one thousand times the Ten Statements of Glorification (Tasbihat), which will be cited within the devotional rites of the ‘Arafat Day.\n2. It is highly recommended to visit the holy tomb of Imam Husayn (a.s.) at the land of Karbala and to reside there up to the ‘Id al-Azha Day (the tenth of Zilhajj) so that Almighty Allah will save from all evils of that year."
